# Three levels (docs/customize/team-cartridge.md, "Checks by gate"): the lines before the first `# level:` marker are a
# task's cheap checks, `# level: phase` is the phase's smoke, run once its tasks have rolled up, and `# level: initiative`
# is the full suite, run before the initiative's one pull request. A file with no marker is all task checks.
#
# Task level: cheap and fast, since every task of a phase runs it at once on one machine. Each component's unit tests,
# from its own folder (their tests import sibling test modules by name), but `# touched only`: a phase-model task runs
# only the test files it added or changed and those whose imports reach a source it changed, and none of a component
# it touched no test of; never a whole suite, which the initiative level runs (E1: three tasks each running all three
# suites timed out). The old model has no wider level, so its flat list leaves these lines out and takes the suites
# whole from the initiative section, as it ran them before levels.
cd src/tools && pytest -q -n auto  # touched only
cd src/graphs && pytest -q -n auto  # touched only
cd src/cartridges && pytest -q -n auto  # touched only
# CI's ruff step, with its safe fixes applied before the gate; the old model leaves it to CI, as it always has.
python -m ruff check .  # fix: python -m ruff check --fix .  # new model only
# CI's "clean (no personal reference)" step, plus a refusal of files under build/.
# --require-names fails the lane when COXSWAIN_CLEAN_DENY is unset, so the names rule is never skipped silently:
# the lane host must export it (the same regex as the CI secret), or a host name passes here and fails CI.
python .github/check_clean.py . --require-names
# H10 item 5 (docs/hardening.md): a public function, class or module the patch adds under src/ with no reference
# outside tests fails the lane; entry points nothing calls by name are allowlisted, with a reason, in .github/unwired-allow.txt.
# An epic lane's base is its phase branch (COX_LANE_BASE, exported by the harness); elsewhere origin/main.
python .github/check_unwired.py
# H2 (docs/hardening.md): the type check, strict on the typed core and basic elsewhere ([tool.pyright] in pyproject.toml).
# Without pyright or the extras in this python it skips and says how to install them, as smoke skips without docker;
# CI sets COX_TYPES_REQUIRED=1, which makes a missing one a failure.
python .github/check_types.py

# level: phase
# The smoke suite without the forge (docs/smoke.md, "The phase check needs no forge"): real cox from this tree against
# real git and a throwaway Postgres container, and no Forgejo. With no docker on PATH it skips and says why (-rs); a
# docker whose daemon does not answer fails unless the host sets COX_SMOKE_SKIP_BROKEN_DOCKER=1.
pytest -q -rs smoke -m "not forge"

# level: initiative
# The full suite, which gates the new model's one pull request (D2: the initiative review's `suite` step, run on the
# worker at the initiative branch's tip before the pull request opens): the three component suites whole, the smoke
# suite with the forge tests, and the umbrella's own tests/. An old-model run reads this file as one flat list, its
# task lines and then these (checks.old_model_checks): exactly the seven commands it ran before levels. The root suite
# is marked `# new model only`, so that list leaves it out: the old model runs it in CI's `unit (root)` job, as it
# always has.
cd src/tools && pytest -q -n auto
cd src/graphs && pytest -q -n auto
cd src/cartridges && pytest -q -n auto
pytest -q -rs smoke
pytest -q -n auto  # new model only
